{"title":"Cohn's criterion","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a prime number, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06932c53df570ab52b94bfcdc71b31238bebc95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> an integer. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/9/3f9ca2d850ff44b0c7041688198c69746aeea235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{p_np_{n-1}\\cdots p_1p_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"14\" /> is the base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> representation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d3a2df02fd44841c21ce73f0924e1c8f9353e69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq p_i&lt;b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"16\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eb6dd7ad75f0e57918a9d2d8c7763e6d7e35cb6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)=p_nx^n+p_{n-1}x^{n-1}+\\cdots+p_1x+p_0\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"19\" />\nis irreducible.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cohn%27s_criterion&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The following proof is due to M. Ram Murty.\n</p><p>We start off with a lemma. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/2/cd26e91c69d156c38e2263725836a88c2fe792e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=a_nx^n+a_{n-1}x^{n-1}+\\cdots+a_1x+a_0\\in \\mathbb{Z}[x]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"375\" height=\"20\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/8/ae89ee73aedf5945473bd7087ffa72e4a2724f39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n\\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/1/711393c58e469f8f11381e508642c36c2836c5b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a_i|\\leq H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. \nThen, any complex root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c175f60eecef1de7560c3bdea495d69f26f719d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, has a non positive real part or satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03e7340843085e92769724407daa794593ead1a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\phi|&lt;\\frac{1+\\sqrt{1+4H}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"150\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Proof: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d6fab49fad48223a8cc7418b656e5435be7b457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> and Re <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/b/c9b762d600896ea82c99d490b90c0c0d11ee4938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, note that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b38098b93c1452f29e5daf5c4a74117842a1059f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|\\frac{g(z)}{z^n}|\\geq |a_n+\\frac{a_{n-1}}{z}|-H(\\frac{1}{|z|^2}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{|z|^n})&gt;Re(a_n+\\frac{a_{n-1}}{z})-\\frac{H}{|z|^2-|z|}\\geq 1-\\frac{H}{|z|^2-|z|}=\\frac{|z|^2-|z|-H}{|z|^2-|z|}\\]\" width=\"782\" height=\"43\" />\nThis means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc88a7d0f2cfb9fc41a2932ee96a02d1964f8c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(z)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/4/a14a9d3b58b1dd176cb28cfb9bb13ebbb0eb0cc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|\\geq \\frac{1+\\sqrt{1+4H}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"153\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03e7340843085e92769724407daa794593ead1a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|\\phi|&lt;\\frac{1+\\sqrt{1+4H}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"150\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/1964a0ff5131884b1940d2f9f61e99e5db8baba9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />, this implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed4c80fde51258e012f032c19c8af613ed33e92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|b-\\phi|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/1964a0ff5131884b1940d2f9f61e99e5db8baba9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b\\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80488c91659d6f179f4eeec6ae9d2ad11faabfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\phi)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea1fb901c032525b58ac56d17256a25d2ba56f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=g(x)h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91e4cc7017746a9ace2030efc4507fdaf0a60be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(b)=p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb92cad72643781b1ec54788224f339c5b315bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|g(b)|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58a06e911d1e83301cc63c7b349164d8f35bde92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is 1. WLOG, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/503f76ebb760f8787012e2f8d67d6b092b42c08e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(b)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a891e16076b78359c63316b3cf72fb779f1ad13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi_1, \\phi_2,\\cdots,\\phi_r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> be the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5aaa1b5a7d69f298fd91e2bf90bc92b7fb58387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|g(b)|=|b-\\phi_1||b-\\phi_2|\\cdots|b-\\phi_r|&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"300\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is irreducible.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/6/7d65baaf9671227780dd04ab952911036aa5c868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, we will need to prove another lemma:\n</p><p>All of the zeroes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> satisfy Re <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/0/b700d3da70821af7603d74e3ae42aaaf4092371c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z&lt;\\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Proof: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, then the two polynomials are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82cfada30c5db524e5c75574bd60707d2d1444e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, both of which satisfy our constraint. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb7ae00764b56ee2adf59e78a1ffde9685b80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, we get the polynomials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/9/dc9a0dfa8d41f77ced12b322e876187b21120e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2\\pm x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/2727209af872821cb6f7d538c343e27ee93a1379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6c5515d3698fd0e95e8c46939c1a99d24c73ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2\\pm x\\pm 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"15\" />, all of which satisfy the constraint. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/811f76ab716762dc2652ba611378a1816b671893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e80839d8d150f76ba8714eafa0969de32d23db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|\\frac{f(z)}{z^n}|\\geq |1+\\frac{a_{n-1}}{z}+\\frac{a_{n-2}}{z^2}|-(\\frac{1}{|z|^3}+\\cdots+\\frac{1}{|z|^n})&gt;|1+\\frac{a_{n-1}}{z}+\\frac{a_{n-2}}{z^2}|-\\frac{1}{|z|^2(|z|-1)}\\]\" width=\"597\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>If Re <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b63c816490cddb2a5da8a3d8b524f846be6ed24b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, we have Re <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/8/b48268988220afb7e38a90eba26d373cec55cb41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{z^2}\\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"37\" />, and then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f0275eb9479bed8648d2efa43e053d16497fc33d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|\\frac{f(z)}{z^n}|&gt;1-\\frac{1}{|z|^2(|z|-1)}\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"43\" />\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/7/a57dc8f3b8b1374b2af2160fe79d5c7177a8cad2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|\\geq \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/d/dcd7ab32b68bdfaab3277e1077f6de9f5df6d273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|^2(|z|-1)\\geq(\\frac{3}{2})^2(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{9}{8}&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"247\" height=\"37\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nTo finish the proof, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea1fb901c032525b58ac56d17256a25d2ba56f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=g(x)h(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386dac64ce375766402d306f6b86213787445b77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)=p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/6/ed6ee027bb5823e31562c577a2c4fa2ab51fcf9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/0115924b8e3e10ca6d47f144474e4a1e6f27d3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is 1. WLOG, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/2/f324962463f3eff3f832618b23b918b6f66876ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(2)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" />. By our lemma, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/610b8fae90ccd281d64450f30d8768ad850107d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z-2|&gt;|z-1|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/8/6a891e16076b78359c63316b3cf72fb779f1ad13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\phi_1, \\phi_2,\\cdots,\\phi_r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10ce2ef400f92ef546d0bea3858fc8598154357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|g(2)|=|2-\\phi_1||2-\\phi_2|\\cdots|2-\\phi_n|&gt;|1-\\phi_1||1-\\phi_2|\\cdots|1-\\phi_n|=|g(1)| &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"606\" height=\"18\" />. This is a contradiction, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is irreducible.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018080643\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 203/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11691/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16650:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018080643 and revision id 148488. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}